<h2>CIPHERA Terms of Service</h2>

<p class="meta">Effective date: {{EFFECTIVE_DATE}} · <a href="terms-ro.html">Versiunea în limba română</a></p>

<p>These terms are an agreement between you and <strong>MSCS di Stefan E.</strong>, {{CONTROLLER_ADDRESS}} ("we"), for the use of the CIPHERA messaging service. The CIPHERA app you download from the App Store is licensed to you under Apple's standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement; if these terms and that licence conflict about the app itself, the licence prevails. How we handle personal data is described in the CIPHERA Privacy Policy.</p>

<h3 id="s1">1. Who may use CIPHERA</h3>

<p>You must be at least 16 years old and able to enter into this agreement. You may not use CIPHERA if the law of your country forbids it.</p>

<h3 id="s2">2. Your account and your keys</h3>

<p>You sign in with Apple or with a one-time code sent to your e-mail address. Your identity keys are created and kept on your devices. We cannot read your messages and <strong>we cannot recover your keys</strong>: if you lose all your devices and have not set up recovery, your identity and your message history cannot be restored. Keep your recovery code private and safe, protect your devices with a passcode, and remove devices you no longer use in Security Center.</p>

<h3 id="s3">3. Subscription and free use through your organization</h3>

<p><strong>3.1 What the subscription covers.</strong> Sending messages, starting conversations, adding contacts, groups, calls and files require an active CIPHERA subscription, unless your account uses CIPHERA free of charge through your organization (3.3). Without either you can still sign in, use Security Center, manage your devices and sessions, set up recovery, sign out, delete your account and read messages already delivered to your device.</p>

<p><strong>3.2 Billing through Apple.</strong> The subscription "CIPHERA" is an auto-renewable subscription sold through the App Store, monthly (CIPHERA Monthly) or yearly (CIPHERA Annual). In the euro area it costs 9.99 € per month or 89.99 € per year; the App Store shows the price for your country before you confirm. Payment is charged to your Apple Account when you confirm the purchase. The subscription <strong>renews automatically</strong> for the same period and price unless you cancel it at least 24 hours before the end of the current period; the renewal is charged within the 24 hours before the period ends. <strong>Cancellation:</strong> you manage and cancel the subscription in your Apple Account settings (on iPhone and iPad: Settings → your name → Subscriptions; on a Mac: App Store → your account → Subscriptions); cancelling stops the next renewal and you keep access until the end of the period already paid. <strong>Refunds</strong> are decided by Apple under its terms; you request one from Apple (reportaproblem.apple.com), not from us. Price changes follow Apple's rules, and Apple tells you about them before they apply. We never receive your payment details. The subscription belongs to your CIPHERA account and works on every device signed in to it, including CIPHERA for Windows, where nothing is sold. Deleting your CIPHERA account does not cancel the subscription: cancel it with Apple.</p>

<p><strong>3.3 Free through your organization.</strong> Organizations can provide CIPHERA to their members by enrolling their e-mail domain with us. If your account's e-mail address — as verified by the sign-in provider (Sign in with Apple when you share your e-mail, or the e-mail code) — is on an enrolled domain, you use CIPHERA free of charge, with nothing to buy or renew. Only an exact domain counts, never a similar-looking one or a private relay address. Free use lasts as long as the domain stays enrolled and your address is on it; if either ends, the features of 3.1 need the subscription from then on. Nothing of your account or your data is deleted by that change, and a subscription you bought earlier is not refunded by us because of it (refunds: 3.2).</p>

<h3 id="s4">4. Acceptable use</h3>

<p>You may not use CIPHERA to:</p>

<ul>
  <li>share material that sexually exploits or endangers children, in any form;</li>
  <li>threaten, harass, bully or intimidate anyone, or encourage violence or self-harm;</li>
  <li>send spam, unsolicited bulk messages or automated messages to people who did not ask for them;</li>
  <li>impersonate a person or an organisation, or mislead people about who you are;</li>
  <li>commit or promote fraud, scams, or any other illegal activity, or distribute malware;</li>
  <li>infringe other people's intellectual property or privacy, including sharing someone's private images without consent;</li>
  <li>probe, attack, overload or reverse-engineer the service's servers, or get around blocks, limits or suspensions.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="s5">5. Blocking, reporting and enforcement</h3>

<p>You can block any account; a blocked account can no longer reach you. You can report an account, a conversation or a message from the app. Because content is end-to-end encrypted, we see only what the reporter chooses to include from their own copy of the conversation. We review reports as quickly as we can, reports about the safety of children first. If we conclude that an account breaks these terms, we may warn it, limit it, suspend it or close it, and where the law requires it we report to the competent authorities. You can contest a decision by writing to {{SUPPORT_EMAIL}}.</p>

<h3 id="s6">6. Your content</h3>

<p>What you send belongs to you or to whoever holds the rights to it. You give us only the permission needed to store and transmit your encrypted data so that it reaches your recipients. We cannot read it and we do not use it for any other purpose.</p>

<h3 id="s7">7. Security limits</h3>

<p>End-to-end encryption protects your communications in transit and on our servers. It cannot protect what is on a device that is lost, unlocked or compromised, or what a recipient chooses to do with a message. Verify your contacts (safety number or QR code) to make sure you are talking to the right person; CIPHERA tells you when a contact's keys change.</p>

<h3 id="s8">8. Changes and availability</h3>

<p>We keep improving CIPHERA and may change or remove features. We aim to keep the service available but cannot guarantee that it will always be available or free of errors. We will tell you in the app before changes to these terms take effect; if you do not agree, you can stop using the service and delete your account.</p>

<h3 id="s9">9. Liability</h3>

<p>Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, in particular for intent, gross negligence, or death or personal injury caused by negligence, or your rights as a consumer. Otherwise, to the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect losses or for losses caused by events outside our reasonable control.</p>

<h3 id="s10">10. Ending the agreement</h3>

<p>You can stop using CIPHERA and delete your account in the app at any time (Settings → Delete account). We may close an account that seriously or repeatedly breaks these terms (section 5). Closing an account does not cancel an App Store subscription; cancel it with Apple (section 3.2).</p>

<h3 id="s11">11. Law</h3>

<p>These terms are governed by the law of {{CONTROLLER_COUNTRY}}. If you are a consumer, you also keep the protection of the mandatory rules of the country where you live, and you may bring a claim in its courts.</p>

<h3 id="s12">12. Contact</h3>

<p>{{SUPPORT_EMAIL}} · MSCS di Stefan E., {{CONTROLLER_ADDRESS}}</p>

